###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# MD speed (atom-timesteps/s) of every linear and quadratic SNAP potential
# versus atom count on one Intel Broadwell node (two 18-core E5-2695v4) is
# shown only in Figure 1; the text gives no per-atom number for SNAP (it
# quotes peak speeds of 5e6 for a MEAM and 5e2 atom-timesteps/s for a GAP
# tungsten potential). Quadratic SNAP is less than twofold slower than
# linear SNAP at equal Jmax.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Introduces quadratic SNAP: 'An extension of the SNAP form is proposed that includes quadratic terms in the bispectrum components' (Abstract; Sec. IV). Recorded in the method registry as qSNAP derived from SNAP.
# - The training energy errors are in eV/atom, for which the vocabulary has no unit individual; mlips:hasUnit is omitted and the unit is in the metric label. The values are the training errors of the unweighted fits used to optimise the cutoff (Tables SI, SII).
# - Force errors, the cutoff scans (Fig. 3) and the cross-validation of the GSF(110) group (Fig. 5) are shown only in figures and not encoded; the group-weight optimisation with a genetic algorithm (DAKOTA) yields potentials whose errors are not tabulated.
# - The DFT settings of the training set are not stated in this paper (they are those of Ref. [19], encoded in thompson2014); the data set therefore carries no reference calculation here.
# - The configuration count (362) is the number of energy training points listed in Sec. V, one per DFT calculation.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/wood2018.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

